From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chinmoy Dey <chinmoy@nexthop.ai>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Report an unknown Switch-Host power state until bmcctld
 publishes it

sonic-dbus-bridge seeds CurrentHostState with a dedicated Unknown value
when HOST_STATE|switch-host does not exist yet, and derives the chassis
power state from it. Stock bmcweb folds any unrecognised host state into
PowerState Off and ignores unrecognised chassis states, so a powered-on
Switch-Host could be reported as Off while bmcctld is still starting.

  - systems.hpp: HostState.Unknown omits PowerState and reports
    Status.State UnavailableOffline instead of Off / Disabled
  - chassis.hpp: PowerState.Unknown omits PowerState and reports
    Status.State UnavailableOffline instead of leaving Enabled

The first HOST_STATE|switch-host row replaces the unknown value on the
bridge and the host state monitor emits the matching ResourceEvent.
---
 redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp |  8 ++++++++
 redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp b/redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp
--- a/redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp
+++ b/redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp
@@ -191,6 +191,15 @@
                     resource::PowerState::Off;
                 asyncResp->res.jsonValue["Status"]["State"] =
                     resource::State::StandbyOffline;
+            }
+            else if (chassisState ==
+                     "xyz.openbmc_project.State.Chassis.PowerState.Unknown")
+            {
+                // sonic-dbus-bridge derives the chassis power state from
+                // the Switch-Host state and reports this until bmcctld has
+                // published HOST_STATE|switch-host: no PowerState claimed.
+                asyncResp->res.jsonValue["Status"]["State"] =
+                    resource::State::UnavailableOffline;
             }
         });
 }
diff --git a/redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp b/redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp
--- a/redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp
+++ b/redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp
@@ -516,6 +516,16 @@
                     resource::PowerState::PoweringOff;
                 asyncResp->res.jsonValue["Status"]["State"] =
                     resource::State::Disabled;
+            }
+            else if (hostState ==
+                     "xyz.openbmc_project.State.Host.HostState.Unknown")
+            {
+                // sonic-dbus-bridge reports this until bmcctld has
+                // published HOST_STATE|switch-host. The Switch-Host may be
+                // on or off, so no PowerState is claimed rather than the
+                // stock fallback to Off.
+                asyncResp->res.jsonValue["Status"]["State"] =
+                    resource::State::UnavailableOffline;
             }
             else
             {
